Proof v2 of the S11-D full journey (J19) failed at two lines; both were spec or
harness defects, not engine ones, and the second is the roster-reader gap the
S11-E src commit (ce37c6ee) closes.

(a) Leg A J17 read terminal readiness with `h.pairCurrent('P2', COACH_A,
    intentId)`: pairCurrent's third argument is the SETUP NONCE, so the read
    looked for a setup that does not exist (404 "Pairing session not found").
    It now uses the nonce-less current-setup read, the live-passing terminal
    precedent of readiness.pg.spec R4 and of J01 in the same leg. The leg A
    empty roster is now discriminated from a blind reader by a direct
    `h.persons(COACH_A)` read (the same read journey-induction and
    settle-redrive make).

(b) test/utils/g2-s11-worker.cjs: roster | entities hand the readers the SAME
    `sourceMappers` the engine planned with (`reconstruct.sourceMappers`, the
    composed A1/A2 registry), the CJS field assignment the engine seam already
    uses. Leg B asserts `accounting.unclassified === 0` beside the staged count
    that failed in proof v2 (0 vs 2), so the fix is observed, not assumed.
    Review B B1 (proof v1 of this spec: `unclassified` 6, not 0): `h.rosterOf`
    carries the single A1-platform REGISTRY, under which none of leg B's
    tokens classify. The leg A and leg B roster reads now go through
    `h.onInduction` (the two-source registry the legs planned with); rosterOf
    / entitiesOf stay on REGISTRY for journey-core, where that seam is right.
    Traced against the induction registry: leg B staged 2, unclassified 0,
    persons = the roster rows' source ids.

(c) J20: SLICE_COMMITS pins ce37c6ee (the S11-E src commit) and the
    full-range walk closes at S11_RANGE_END = ce37c6ee instead of HEAD; the
    ancestor check covers the range end. Every src-touching commit in
    3db615c0^..ce37c6ee is pinned and none carries a source slug. The
    comment describing the full-range walk names S11_RANGE_END, not HEAD.
